%% Customer chat and tenant-scoped support conversation
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Customer
    participant Web as Customer Web/BFF
    participant REST as Chat REST API
    participant Auth as Tenant membership/participant policy
    participant DB as Tenant PostgreSQL
    participant Queue as Chat notification queue
    participant Gateway as Socket.IO gateway
    participant Redis
    participant Agent as Tenant support agent

    Customer->>Web: Open support chat on tenant host
    Web->>REST: Request guest or authenticated socket ticket
    REST->>Auth: Validate tenant context and actor/guest policy
    Auth-->>Web: Short-lived tenant-bound ticket
    Web->>Gateway: Connect and authenticate ticket
    Gateway->>Redis: Register tenant-scoped presence

    Customer->>REST: Create/find conversation
    REST->>Auth: Verify participant membership or support policy
    Auth->>DB: Read/write conversation membership
    DB-->>REST: Conversation identity
    REST-->>Web: Conversation and cursor metadata

    Customer->>REST: POST message
    REST->>Auth: Verify participant and sender ownership
    REST->>DB: Transactionally persist message and last-message state
    DB-->>REST: Durable message
    REST->>Queue: Enqueue participant notification after commit
    REST->>Gateway: Ask gateway to emit through organization-scoped room
    Gateway->>Redis: Fan out tenant-scoped event
    Gateway-->>Agent: New message event
    Queue-->>Agent: Notification delivery work

    Agent->>REST: Read, update, or delete own permitted message
    REST->>Auth: Recheck participant and sender ownership
    REST->>DB: Apply cursor/ownership-safe mutation
    REST->>Gateway: Ask gateway to emit updated tenant-scoped event

    Note over DB,Queue: Notifications reference a durable message; a rolled-back message is not notified.
    Note over Gateway,Redis: Identical conversation IDs in different tenants use different room namespaces.
